In the man outside the window scenario there are three ways to interpret 
the situation:
	1. Believe that the man is outside the window. (faith)
	2. Believe that the man is not outside the window. (aetheism)
	3. Believe that there is no way of telling (whether there is no proof 
now, or the proof is impossible to find altogether), and therefore the 
existence of the man outside the window is unimportant. (agnosticism)



