I think the dispute is not about logic, but rather the definition of 
words. If the pragmatic atheist claims that he does not believe in god, 
but he also does not believe in the non-existence of god, then he is not 
an atheist.

When asked the question "Does god exist?" the archetypal response from 
believers, atheists and agnostics is:

believer: Yes
atheist: No
agnostic: I don't know

Atheism is believing there is no god, not disbelieving that there is a 
god, and in this way atheism and agnosticism are mutually exclusive.


